{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/molliecomponents"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","externalID":"MollieComponents","title":"MollieComponents","modules":[{"name":"MollieComponents"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MollieComponents"},{"type":"text","text":" is the merchant-facing entry point to the Mollie Components iOS SDK. You present a payment surface — modal or embedded — hand it a server-issued client access token, and receive a single typed "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePaymentResult"},{"type":"text","text":" describing how the flow ended. The card number and CVC the cardholder types are captured inside Mollie’s own UI and tokenized over TLS; they never cross the documented SDK boundary into your code. Your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onResult"},{"type":"text","text":" callback receives only session metadata, never raw card data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"3D Secure is handled for you. When the issuer requires a challenge, the SDK presents the authentication WebView, drives it to a terminal state, and folds the outcome back into the same ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePaymentResult","type":"reference"},{"text":" you already handle — there is no separate 3DS callback to wire up.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK runs inside your app’s process. UIKit provides no platform-level isolation between your code and the SDK, so the protection of typed card data is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"contractual, not platform-enforced"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Read "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SECURITY.md"},{"type":"text","text":" at the repository root for the full trust model — what the SDK defends against, what it cannot enforce, and the integration practices your team must follow."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To get going in a few lines, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/GettingStarted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". To map every outcome the SDK can hand back to merchant-facing behavior, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/HandlingErrors","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Getting-Started","title":"Getting Started","identifiers":["doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MollieCheckout"]},{"anchor":"Presenting","title":"Presenting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MollieCheckout","doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MollieCardComponent"]},{"anchor":"Results","title":"Results","identifiers":["doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePaymentResult","doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePayment"]},{"anchor":"Appearance","title":"Appearance","identifiers":["doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/Theming"]},{"anchor":"Configuration","title":"Configuration","identifiers":["doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MollieEndpoints"]},{"anchor":"Handling-Errors","title":"Handling Errors","identifiers":["doc:\/\/build.MollieComponents\/documentati